From 12d7699748b7943510dbcc452d0cfc9c262ef757 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@y.z>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:11:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/21] devices: add polled Qualcomm GENI debug UART driver

FIFO-mode 8N1 driver for the qcom,geni-debug-uart serial engine behind a
small Mmio trait. init() checks the SE firmware protocol at
GENI_FW_REVISION_RO (0x68), quiesces running TX/RX commands, programs
packing, watermarks, FIFO mode and frame format, and restarts the RX
sequencer. The serial clock divider is only written when the SE clock
rate is known; otherwise the firmware setting is kept, as Linux earlycon
does. TX is one command per byte with bounded polls and an abort path;
RX drains packed FIFO words honouring RX_LAST_BYTE_VALID. SE interrupt
delivery stays masked because the GIC virq for SPI 354 does not fit the
u8 numbering the console IRQ handler passes to irq_trigger.

Host tests run against a behavioural register model.

Co-Authored-By: Cursor <noreply@cursor.com>
